#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# up_values

#% text
# `up_values(g)` gives the rules attached to `g` with `@on(g)`: rules for calls of another head that have `g(...)` or `g` among their arguments (semantics 6.5), as `lhs :> rhs` with the left side as it was written.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
@on(square) rule area(square(a_)) := a^2

#% cell
up_values(square)
#% output
#= [area(square(a_)) :> a^2]

#% text
# The rule is stored with `square`, not with `area`:

#% cell
down_values(area)
#% output
#= []

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `down_values`, `sub_values`, `own_values`
